  "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\pi }(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x))=$",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x):$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14189988/assets/0fa9338fbefb3682249a585b85d287a25868a8f137547830adf6085dae85139a.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Moreover, from the graph, we see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)=\\pi .\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\pi }(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x))=\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot (\\pi )=1.\n$$",
